e  to stay for tonight or  for as long as needed  i will say many people that maybe place  i'm sorry i won't put a number to it but  we know that there are people that are  displaced can you speak to the  structural integrity of the buildings  downtown as given the explosion  is that part of the reason why there's a  curfew for the next few days to make  in case anything collapses absolutely so  at the office of emergency management  when we try to look at the overall view  of the city and making sure that  everything is safe and working together  the we know we had one building collapse  due to the explosion and due to the age  of the other buildings and then we had  water  was being actually displayed throughout  the buildings and with the cold weather  we thank the water department as well  making sure that they've got the water  shut off but still the integrity of  those buildings are in question so we're  trying to make sure  that we do have everybody in place and  um  safety for our personnel what building  that was what building  was that collapsed i don't have that  address i'm sorry  business was inside residential or  anything yeah it was a it was a building  that actually  housed across from the explosion which  above the it was residential above  so i can't really give you that i'm  sorry all right guys  thank you our last question for this  evening i want to thank you guys for  coming out we will be in touch with you  with regular updates  again thank you to mayor cooper to chief  swan and chief drake for being here and  especially to those  officers that we are so grateful for  this evening  you'll hear from us again all right  thank you  okay  i

